# BusinessPilot AI

BusinessPilot AI is an enterprise-style multi-agent system for customer churn prediction, retention planning, and business workflow automation. The repository combines a FastAPI service, orchestration agents, memory support, and evaluation logic into a practical capstone implementation that can be extended for real-world customer success workflows.

## Overview

This project demonstrates how multiple specialized agents can collaborate to:
- score customer churn risk from business context,
- generate explainable retention recommendations,
- build structured action plans,
- persist customer sessions and interaction history,
- evaluate the quality of the recommendations.

The current implementation centers on a lightweight but extensible architecture that is suitable for both local development and future cloud deployment.

## Key Capabilities

- Multi-agent orchestration for churn analysis and retention planning
- FastAPI-based service layer with session and scoring endpoints
- Memory-backed session management for conversational or iterative workflows
- Evaluation framework for basic business KPI tracking
- Modular structure for future integration with external tools and models

## Project Structure

- [docs](docs) – architecture and usage documentation
- [src](src) – application code for agents, services, models, and data utilities
- [tests](tests) – automated verification for core components
- [deployment](deployment) – deployment notes and infrastructure guidance
- [configs](configs) – configuration and environment references

## Quick Start

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/jcdumlao14/ai-agents-vibe-capstone.git
cd ai-agents-vibe-capstone
```

### 2. Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 3. Start the API server

```bash
uvicorn src.services.api:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
```

### 4. Run the test suite

```bash
pytest
```

## Example Usage

Health check:

```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
```

Score a customer:

```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/score \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "customer_id": "cust_001",
    "usage": 18.5,
    "support_tickets": 3,
    "contract_months_remaining": 1
  }'
```

